// The bestiary expansion (Nov 2026): 67 new species, each in three forms (201
// monsters), and 20 new bosses, spread over every region and level band.
//
// This file is data only (it imports nothing, so npcs.js, sprites.js and
// slayer.js can all read it without an import cycle). npcs.js builds the
// monsters and bosses from it with the same makeMob / makeBoss as everything
// else; world.js places them last, on a stream of their own (bestiaryPlace.js),
// so nothing already in the world moves. Their signature moves, mechanics and
// signature weapons are appended to bossAbilities.js, bossMechanics.js and
// bossWeapons.js like the earlier bosses'.
//
// No painted art exists for them yet: each borrows a close relative's picture
// (`borrow`: a species family or a boss id that has art) recoloured with a CSS
// filter (`tint`), until its own arrives. `look` is the brief for the artist
// (docs/bestiary-expansion.json is generated from it); `lore` is the Monster
// Codex's description.

// Level bands (old loot-tier levels) of the starting island's regions, which
// have none of their own in world.js. The new monsters and bosses keep inside them.
export const ISLAND_BANDS = {
  'Bukit Timah': [5, 60], 'MacRitchie Reservoir': [5, 45], 'Sentosa Beach': [8, 48],
  'The Wilderness': [30, 124], 'Pulau Hantu': [40, 124],
};

